  "differences": [
    {
      "what": "Directly reviewed actual full source and current thirty-member native pair, 2026-11-10. Kurz panel1 clusters its cupola towers toward the curtain centre and compresses range overlap; the current fort retains Whistler's measured corner blockhouses, range functions/lengths and plan under the explicit T3335 owner ruling. This is a conflict between retrospective composition and the adopted contemporary plan, not a missing/wrongly placed model element. T3153 makes source/plan/camera disagreement within tolerance; no surveyed member is moved and no whole-panel metric equivalence is claimed.",
      "status": "within tolerance"
    },
    {
      "what": "The full source visibly includes an unlabelled two-storey galleried house outside the stockade at lower right. No source-specific identification ties that form to any of these30named records. The contextual render does not establish such an identity; it must not relabel the agent, factory, house-in-factor-department, stable or another context member merely to fill that silhouette. This is not individually shown for a named component, not an established missing named building. The existing plan/text records remain intact; no new anonymous house is asserted.",
      "status": "not shown"
    },
